osw hostap: restart the BSS for a channel change hostapd cannot switch to

opensync-rpi / opensync-lab: a channel change that confsync marks CSA-eligible was
applied only as hostapd's CHAN_SWITCH, and only on phys configured for it
(OSW_DRV_NL80211_CSA_IMPL_PHY_<phy>=..._HOSTAP; the cfg80211 platform's 50_owm.conf
names phy0-phy2). On the Raspberry Pi pods (MT7921U, an AP sharing its radio with the
backhaul station), hostapd answers CHAN_SWITCH with FAIL; the reply was not checked,
so the AP stayed on its old channel while its station followed the root AP to another
(ACS moved the physical MV3 from 6 to 2 to 10): its clients could not associate,
confsync re-requested the change every minute, never settled, and its watchdog
aborted owm every 3 minutes. On a phy without the setting (phy3 onwards: a replugged
adapter, or mac80211_hwsim radios) the change was never applied at all.

The BSS is now removed and added again on the new channel (a few seconds without the
AP) when hostapd refused the last CSA, or when the phy has no CSA implementation;
CSA stays the way when it works. The decision is in osw_hostap_csa.h, free of
osw_hostap's state, so that pod/opensync/tests/osw_hostap_csa_test.c tests it on its
own. The glue (the refusal recorded from CHAN_SWITCH's reply, cleared when the BSS is
added) is proven live by an AP following its station's channel move: pending on
2026-10-09, when the MV3's image V45 cut the Raspberry Pi pods' LAN side at 09:00Z
(not the patch), and to come from the Pis and from opensync-lab's chain room.

Upstream: an OpenSync core bug as released in 6.6.1.0: osw_hostap_bss_hapd_csa() in
src/lib/osw/src/osw_hostap.c queues CHAN_SWITCH without checking its reply, and the
config path's "invalidated"/"do_csa" leave a CSA-eligible channel change unapplied
when CSA is not available. Not reported (the owner decides).

